    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "block-sparse-mlp",
        "title": "Explicit routing policy and configurable correction-bias lookup",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Construction accepts router_type='std', 'ds3' or 'dots', stores the corresponding function in routing_fn, and rejects other names. forward invokes that function before the unchanged ordinary-versus-fused expert dispatch.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_81e6e71f8d3148f6b87ff7237fcd5fe5",
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Whole-parent searches locate three BlockSparseMLP builders. Dots1 migrates its explicit boolean to router_type='dots'; Mixtral and Qwen3 MoE omit both options and therefore accept the new standard default. All use keyword arguments. No other reader of the removed deepseekv3_routing attribute was found.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9bc97b31ff184145b852f24b1e44bd96",
              "call_cbd4785778184157a6d51801f2539674",
              "call_c9df1622cbd6435f948abc20717a258a",
              "call_b61e9be6b8004e7aba829c685a1e8936",
              "call_c27e25a6216f48fe8dc7fd3488a69d32",
              "call_39c773ea018d479d895c92eaead89ce2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "routing_std is the renamed existing Python helper, previously only referenced by a commented call. Like the replaced native router, it projects token rows, selects top-k logits and softmax-normalizes selected values. One flattened token without activate_all_experts reuses output buffers; otherwise it allocates results and can select every expert. This removes a native boundary but establishes no speed improvement.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_aceb8f60edb7432ea33f65216c1dd2a8",
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7",
              "call_5105d179a15240098c17a63380ab6ed9",
              "call_81e6e71f8d3148f6b87ff7237fcd5fe5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "routing_dots adds correction bias to logits before top-k and sigmoid normalization. routing_ds3 instead adds bias to sigmoid scores for selection, scores each group by its best two corrected scores, masks unselected groups and gathers uncorrected sigmoid weights. DS3 therefore requires divisible group sizes and at least two experts per group. Both sigmoid routes normalize with a 1e-20 denominator stabilizer and multiply by routed_scaling_factor.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Explicit DS3 selection removes the earlier unassigned-routing-results branch, but does not validate DS3 inputs. Previously the sole active Dots call required n_group=topk_group=1; Dots1 already supplies those values. The new selector calls each helper directly, without adding argument preparation or missing-bias handling.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b49a425f23454025a9134f286ecc1a6d",
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7",
              "call_c9df1622cbd6435f948abc20717a258a",
              "call_81e6e71f8d3148f6b87ff7237fcd5fe5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "key_e_score_bias changes the optional tensor lookup to <module key>.<configured suffix>, falling back to gate.e_score_correction_bias for a missing or empty suffix. RoutingCFG receives the loaded tensor as before. get_tensors remains on the hard-coded old suffix, so custom lookup and export naming disagree.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ca5acb4c60444928bb91b4f2159794d8",
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7",
              "call_81e6e71f8d3148f6b87ff7237fcd5fe5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Both dots-studio/dots.llm1.base and dots-studio/dots.llm1.inst configurations specify 128 routed experts, six selected experts, hidden size 4096, expert width 1408 and scale 2.5. Both select one initial dense layer, overriding the source defaults of eight selected experts and three dense layers. Their routing configuration agrees with Dots1's unchanged single-group construction.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4da986062a544be4aae5fc7708581314",
              "call_84bf18eb6abe4799aabb2c5362a41e90",
              "call_c9df1622cbd6435f948abc20717a258a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Representative base-checkpoint headers contain model.layers.1.mlp.gate.e_score_correction_bias [128] and gate.weight [128,4096], matching the unchanged default lookup and expert count. Expert gate/up weights are [1408,4096], down weights [4096,1408], and shared gate/up weights [2816,4096]. The unchanged default path needs no alternate bias name; custom suffix presence is caller-dependent. Attention and dense-layer tensors in these headers are not read by BlockSparseMLP itself.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_fcf75cda289f422498937506fcab66a7",
              "call_95c6481c099a4a8aa77a6d6b42a90309",
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7",
              "call_c9df1622cbd6435f948abc20717a258a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A scalar transcription with logits [2,1,0] and two selected experts produced standard weights approximately [0.731059,0.268941], summing to 1, versus zero-bias Dots weights [1.366123,1.133877], summing to scale 2.5. Integer shape arithmetic also confirmed that 128 all-expert indices cannot satisfy a six-plane fused-output equality check.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5a10fa49ae2941aeb17d2a5584be092b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The all-expert fused-buffer mismatch and workspace-backed fused return recorded by earlier entries remain unchanged. The grouped unassigned-variable defect is removed by explicit dispatch, while optional Dots inputs remain unguarded. TransformerBlock forwards params and immediately consumes the MLP result; ParallelDecoderBlock has another generic call but does not declare BlockSparseMLP among its constructor types.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ab4f548364dc435cbd9361ef76fa8da7",
              "call_81e6e71f8d3148f6b87ff7237fcd5fe5",
              "call_4c733e3b50b0424d976290d20d714723",
              "call_903aaa9f1efa43d485b1d94a18379f9a"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
